                            <a name="comment2859"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: The Whirlwind
</h4>

<p>
As much as we writers don&#8217;t like the fact that we&#8217;re no longer the last word on a subject, I don&#8217;t know that it&#8217;s necessarily a bad thing. Those who have heard me complain about the comments on the Record Web site know I&#8217;m not a huge fan of reader posts. But I also don&#8217;t think it&#8217;s fair for us to deny others a right to comment and, yes, bash, the story or even our writing and reporting, especially our subjects themselves.<br />
<br />
We have to remember we don&#8217;t just write stories, we write about people, their lives and their families. And while it might be just another clip for our books, what we write affects them personally so they have every right to comment about the things we publish about them. After all we&#8217;ve been enjoying our monopoly on the conversation for a long time, maybe it&#8217;s time we relinquish some of that power.
</p>
